83c4fb6bcc94d" "q-91159/selection/203c73de8727b7d1e651451b600fdf4ba56310ed57ccae98bd6ae3f9fb4c47c3" "q-91159/selection/daf99536256f992e8d34cec82e5ab6b0c320614b0359f958419098aea75d4f4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-91159" :question/id #uuid "26e3c3e9-0f2f-55d8-b677-4d51648ddadf" :question/math-academy-id "q-91159" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{21}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91159/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-91159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-91158/selection/6b77402f20daabb37931fc3d6ea41ba284992c084895c3bfefc3adab49982d6c" :answer/id #uuid "ee300c0c-04be-5284-9ce9-ac24b4c22bbb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}$"