c25-22f5-53f0-9cda-6998f9be7e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-91158" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 21\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91158/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-91158"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448/selection/9c1be975dd0b4359eaefdddedbe56944b346edccd8e46efffc71769fc7282a65" :answer/id #uuid "fc48bf2d-7f94-563e-84b8-38654a77deda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448/selection/301a8c50a1c121602833fd2c2a480a565278d3cf7a84d224900bd7f7606cffc4" :answer/id #uuid "c0459213-0b6c-5853-a3c3-fe1a564f35d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448/selection/05c454345e5efc57f0558a1f1be6afdc94d8f5f9c1cfc580f191e88ce9700322" :answer/id #uuid "1b8c1eae-857c-5731-8285-91d6f4afe9dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448/selection/ab5e65e40823d9b431d67ef45042c578283f7246b670bc6c6e64c6e6dc49c9b0" :answer/id #uuid "b1c8e53e-72f8-569c-9340-0493c4ee85af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448/selection/efa669cba22e54487bcd53d1e9a0da6862c04eb0634c337184b27bee991db9d5" :answer/id #uuid "998870eb-7619-55c8-bf90-f1026375a37a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1d2c21d-93cf-5c6e-9f64-17ddcfb69439" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130448/selection/efa669cba22e54487bcd53d1e9a0da6862c04eb0634c337184b27bee991db9d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-130448/selection/9c1be975dd0b4359eaefdddedbe56944b346edccd8e46efffc71769fc7282a65" "q-130448/selection/301a8c50a1c121602833fd2c2a480a565278d3cf7a84d224900bd7f7606cffc4" "q-130448/selection/05c454345e5efc57f0558a1f1be6afdc94d8f5f9c1cfc580f191e88ce9700322" "q-130448/selection/ab5e65e40823d9b431d67ef45042c578283f7246b670bc6c6e64c6e6dc49c9b0" "q-130448/selection/efa669cba22e54487bcd53d1e9a0da6862c04eb0634c337184b27bee991db9d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130448" :question/id #uuid "fc4fe478-ecca-5d83-9a4b-47e34a0bc1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130448" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{12}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130448/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130448"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130451/selection/b340902c7fa66330570479ea0b47b3f4116154b0089901115d55ddb4e6238fc0" :answer/id #uuid "05d62c28-3fc6-5415-b059-6f59b5077c6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130451/selection/8c8bc85d307936521a65da15c031b008438d51a7eb0a6ee795645373ff2cfffd" :answer/id #uuid "db49b698-4c11-5e23-a25e-1c2ec8662450" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130451/selection/f2c3b33d65512e91c07676c60ed7241082e709ff6e16947a51d22ff873e54587" :answer/id #uuid "11f2b5f1-d225-5660-83d5-7248cb2335f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}