missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below ${a}_{24}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -10 & -3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 13 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -10 & -3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 13 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 9 & 11 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 13 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 9 & 11 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 13 & 17 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-91179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-91179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130462/selection/100dc5036b1b0491faac0892592103f7bf6ca75c7478bd15737b40b296bc374c" :answer/id #uuid "4b26501a-2916-57ce-8869-36d0d0fc6a16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130462/selection/fc09d3476e02e4e545d9f7fc316a2ed1145e1277649105dc1cf30f3b1741f073" :answer/id #uuid "3d395ac5-4c44-5153-9c32-4eddad2a6e52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130462/selection/96b18a6bb8866c8bd040c