nsure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130611" :question/id #uuid "0a755768-3d53-55e9-9809-6ee600be38a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130611" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130611/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85e1fe3f-e85e-5ab4-a594-c55b84bb789a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130611"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-91186/selection/4e29469899c3f9f201c5fdcd64954b2453ed4bbe7382e6acae9b9b78801ce415" :answer/id #uuid "636235b0-1734-547f-8bf7-19d38658f54c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91186/selection/ee2d31cd7f5ebf2f54bd871937280984904dfd89003e53c7d4cef6db89797f54" :answer/id #uuid "5d61265f-36a3-57f9-a22b-3773d4b